#: src/extensions/themes.md:3
msgid "Themes"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:5
msgid ""
"The `themes` directory in an extension should contain one or more theme "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:7
msgid ""
"Each theme file should adhere to the JSON schema specified at [`https://zed."
"dev/schema/themes/v0.2.0.json`](https://zed.dev/schema/themes/v0.2.0.json)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:9
msgid ""
"See [this blog post](https://zed.dev/blog/user-themes-now-in-preview) for "
"additional background on creating themes."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:11
msgid "Theme JSON Structure"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:13
msgid ""
"The structure of a Zed theme is defined in the [Zed Theme JSON Schema]"
"(https://zed.dev/schema/themes/v0.2.0.json)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:15
msgid "A Zed theme consists of a Theme Family object including:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:17
msgid "`name`: The name for the theme family"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:18
msgid "`author`: The name of the author of the theme family"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:19
msgid "`themes`: An array of Themes belonging to the theme family"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:21
msgid "The core components of a Theme object include:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:23
msgid "Theme Metadata:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:25
msgid "`name`: The name of the theme"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:26
msgid "`appearance`: Either \"light\" or \"dark\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:28
msgid "Style Properties under the `style`, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:30
msgid "`background`: The main background color"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:31
msgid "`foreground`: The main text color"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:32
msgid "`accent`: The accent color used for highlighting and emphasis"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:34
msgid "Syntax Highlighting:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:36
msgid ""
"`syntax`: An object containing color definitions for various syntax elements "
"(e.g., keywords, strings, comments)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:38
msgid "UI Elements:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:40
msgid "Colors for various UI components such as:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:41
msgid "`element.background`: Background color for UI elements"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:42
msgid ""
"`border`: Border colors for different states (normal, focused, selected)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:43
msgid "`text`: Text colors for different states (normal, muted, accent)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:45
msgid "Editor-specific Colors:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:47
msgid "Colors for editor-related elements such as:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:48
msgid "`editor.background`: Editor background color"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:49
msgid "`editor.gutter`: Gutter colors"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:50
msgid "`editor.line_number`: Line number colors"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:52
msgid "Terminal Colors:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:53
msgid "ANSI color definitions for the integrated terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:55
msgid "Designing Your Theme"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:57
msgid ""
"You can use [Zed's Theme Builder](https://zed.dev/theme-builder) to design "
"your own custom theme based on an existing one."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/themes.md:59
msgid ""
"This tool lets you fine-tune and preview how surfaces in Zed will look. You "
"can then export the JSON and publish it in Zed's extension store."
msgstr ""
